# The build context is sent to the Docker daemon in full on every build, and
# `COPY . .` bakes whatever survives into the image. Without this file that was
# 247MB, 226MB of it host-built node_modules — which the image cannot use
# anyway: `npm ci` reinstalls them, and native modules like @node-rs/argon2 are
# compiled for the host, not for the Linux image.
node_modules
npm-debug.log

# Build output — regenerated inside the image by `npm run build`.
build
.svelte-kit

.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.vscode

# Secrets never belong in an image layer. The compose file and Railway supply
# the real values as environment variables.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Reference material that ships with the repo but has no business in the image.
*.pptx
*.pdf
*.xlsx
*.jpeg
*.jpg
*.png
docs
integrations
ESS portal design system
ESS portal design system (6)

Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
README.md
PRODUCT.md
